These  objectives  will  be  implemented  by  a  supervisory  system  that  is  based  on  a  functionally  and geographically  distributed  microprocessor-based  plant  level  controllers  using  redundant  architecture techniques. The redundancy shall be complete including the processors, interface main communication module, power supply modules, station bus. The man machine Interface (MMI) in the control room shall include all necessary visual display units, keyboards and other devices required to operate, configure and
monitor  the  Facility.  The  number  of  hard-wired  and/or  conventional  instruments  shall  be  minimised commensurate with safety and legal requirements; in particular, the Contractor shall provide hard-wired pushbutton switches for  emergency  shutdown  of  each  gas  turbine  and  each  steam  turbine.  Moreover, where equipment presents a danger to people (e.g. rotary screens), the Contractor shall provide local hardwired pushbutton switches in general in accordance with any legal requirements.
A  consistent  instrumentation  and  control  philosophy  shall  apply  throughout  the  plant  and  shall  be implemented in terms of a range of equipment exhibiting a minimum diversity of type and manufacturer. The objective shall be to standardize measurement and control equipment throughout the plant in order to rationalize operation, maintenance and reduce spares holding.
The  main  items  of  plant  such  as  the  GTs,  steam  turbines,  water  treatment  etc.  may  be  supplied  with proprietary,  purpose-designed,  systems  for  control,  monitoring  and  protection.  Such  systems  shall  be designed to function independently of each other but shall be interfaced to the supervisory level to allow co-ordinated operation of the Facility. The system shall have a high level of availability. As the C&I system employs  duplication  of  facilities  at  the  supervisory  and  MMI  levels  and  they  must  be  unitised  at  the automation (plant) level, no single C&I failure shall:
- Cause danger to personnel, environment and plant;
- Invalidate protection by inhibiting a trip or interlock (except on minor plant items);
- Shut down more than one major plant item (equipment or machine);
- Simultaneously trip a plant item and invalidate it's auto-change-over;
- Cause a control failure and simultaneously inhibit protection;
- Cause a control failure and simultaneously inhibit the alarm indicating the consequent condition of the plant;
- Affect more than one control area.
There shall be no single common cause failure possibilities (e.g. air supplies, static switches, fuel supply etc.).  The  automation  level  outstations  shall  be  able  to  continue  to  operate  safely  in  the  event  of communication failure and/or failure of the supervisory level. Safety critical inter-trips  between plant sections shall be hard wired in addition to any protection relying on data communication (and must meet the single failure criteria above). This shall be achieved by the use of redundant design techniques and equipment.
The interface point is the interface panel(s) provided as part of the Interface Room in Grid Station and power plant Interface Room:

Thermocouples (if used) will be dual-element, grounded, spring-loaded, Chromel-Constantan (ANSI Type E) for general service. Thermocouple heads will be the cast type with an internal grounding screw. If a thermocouple is inaccessible, the leads will be brought to a junction box in an accessible location. Where thermocouples are employed then cold junction compensation may be provided as per manufacturer's standards  practice.  For  Turbine/Generator  set  OEM  standard  and  general  industrial  practice  are acceptable.
Where ASME Performance Test Codes (e.g., PTC-6 Steam Turbines) are applicable to power cycle piping, they will be used as the criteria for determining well lengths.
Inside GT package, standard specification of thermocouples/RTD's is as follows;
- Thermocouple;
Type E, manufacturer's standard element diameter, ungrounded, double element, 316 stainless steel sheath, manufacturer's standard terminal head with screw type terminal block inside and terminal head cap with chain
Accuracy (tolerance) of thermocouples will conform to ASTM E230 special.
- RTD;
Pt 100 ohm, 3-wire, ungrounded, double element, 316 stainless steel sheath, manufacturer's standard terminal head with screw type terminal block inside and terminal head cap with chain, mounting on thermowell or protection tube
Accuracy (tolerance) of RTD's will conform to ASTM E1137 Class A.
Temperature measuring devices will be installed in thermowells or protection tubes except for such as devices mounted on the turbine and metal temperature measurement.

