HMI shall be possible to display the process with corresponding graphic displays, control loop displays, electrical single line schematics, group displays, etc., all with dynamically updated process parameters on the video display units ('VDU'). The system shall be able to create and to show displays like the following:
- -Overview display;
- -Process graphic display;
- -Alarm summary display;
- -Loop display;
- -Sequence control status display;
- -Trend display (real time and historical trends); and
- -Logging reports.
The human machine interface ('HMI') system shall be capable of processing all inputs in such a manner that all displayed data shall be updated within typical one (1) second for analogue and digital inputs. The system must be capable of accepting spontaneous events from the process with a time resolution of 100 ms  (1ms  for  sequence  of  event  recording  ('SER'  function),  independent  from  the  above  mentioned scanning cycle times.
Abnormal operating conditions and events in the Plant have to be annunciate. Under operation control, it shall be possible to print all or selected alarms on demand.
I&C systems shall be designed in such a way that the Plant can be remotely controlled from the central control  room  ('CCR')  during  start  up,  normal  operation  and  shut  down.  Local  activities  shall  be  not necessary, except after long term outages.
The  operation  concept  shall  consider  in  the  CCR  at  least  four  (4)  operator  stations  for  each  power generation  control  desk  (one  per  Plant  Unit)  as  well  as  large  screen  projection  and  another  four  (4) Operator stations for the common and electrical services control desk. In addition, each one (1) operator station with access to supervise all Plant Units and systems shall be foreseen for the shift leader and in the superintendent's office. Each operator station shall be equipped with two (2) VDUs.

The CCR shall include a dedicated site emergency panel with all functions hard wired from the field and these  signals  shall  also  be  duplicated  on  the  control  system  and  shall  include  (without  limitation)  the following:
- Gas and steam turbine emergency trip;
- Auxiliary boiler emergency trip;
- Generating unit trip button and ESD trips;
- Firefighting system;
- Gas pipeline shutoff valve.
Components  being  of  high  importance  for  safe  operation  like  burner  management  system  or  general boiler/plant  protection  are  to  be  realized  with  fail-safe  technique.  Single  fault  tolerant  design  shall  be provided to avoid tripping of a boiler or turbine as a result of malfunction of the protection equipment.
Permissive interlocks shall be active at all levels to prevent incorrect operation of the and to ensure a high level of integrity of operation. Interlocks shall be capable of being tested with the equipment in operation. The protection and interlocks systems shall incorporate comprehensive diagnostics to input level and shall
be visible during the start-up and shut-down sequences via the control system displays for troubleshooting purposes.
As a general rule, measuring points and measuring equipment for interlocking and protection purposes shall  be  separated  and  not  combined  with  measuring  equipment  for  monitoring  or  automatic  control equipment. For flow measurements one common primary element can be used.
Components  being  of  high  importance  for  safe  operation  like  burner  management  system  or  general boiler/Plant  protection  shall  be  realized  with  fail-safe  technique.  Single  fault  tolerant  design  shall  be provided to avoid tripping of a boiler or turbine as a result of malfunction of the protection equipment.
The process requires an evaluation to determine the appropriate independent protection layers ('IPL') to control  hazards.  Safety  instrumented  systems  ('SIS')  are  intended  to  provide  protection  for  people, property and the environment against deviations in the processes. IEC 61508 and IEC 61511 standards shall be followed to determine, design and build independent protection layers and safety instrumented systems. Every safety related loop has to be verified according to the standards IEC 61508 and IEC 61511 that the requested and necessary safety integrated level ('SIL') is fulfilled for the individual loop. The EPC has to assess all safety related loops to ensure compliance with the related requirements and has to make a protocol about these studies.

