- a) Low-reactance current transformer . All current transformers are in line with IEC 61869-2. A current transformer shall be deemed to have low-reactance performance, without test of further proof, provided:
- i. that the core is of the jointless ring type;
- ii. that  the  secondary  turns  are  substantially  evenly  distributed  along  the  whole  length  of  the magnetic circuit except that a circumferential spacing not exceeding 19 mm on the outer periphery or subtending an angle not exceeding 30°, whichever is the greater, shall be permissible between the two ends of the winding;
- iii. that the primary conductor passes through the approximate centre of the core aperture, and
- iv. that there is normal spacing between adjacent phase conductors.
Unless otherwise indicated, post-type current transformers satisfying requirements i. and ii. above shall be deemed to be of the low-reactance type without test or further proof.
- b) High impedance relay circuit . This is defined as a relay or relay circuit whose setting voltage is not less than the calculated maximum voltage which can appear across its terminals under the assigned maximum through-fault condition, it being assumed that:
- i. there  is  a  complete  saturation  of  the  current  transformer  having  the  highest  loop-resistance including its own secondary winding resistance between it and the relay circuit terminals;
- ii. the  primary  winding  of  this  current  transformer  carries  the  assigned  maximum  through  fault current and

- i. the nominal current settings of the relay together with the maximum VA consumption of the relay at those settings;
- ii. the prescribed current setting (i.e. the setting to be used with the particular equipment concerned) and
- iii. the design values, with tolerances, of all external ancillary apparatus.

- i. the  nominal  voltage  settings  of  the  relay  with  all  series-connected  ancillary  apparatus (internal or external) in circuit, together with the maximum relay operating current at those settings;
- ii. the prescribed voltage setting (i.e. the setting to be used with the particular equipment concerned) and
- iii. the design values, with tolerances, of any shunt connected ancillary apparatus.
